n-voter, a reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"rationale\": \"The public VerifyLeader contract and the suffrage contract jointly require voter-quorum confirmation. The implementation appears to register every replication stream, including non-voters, on the same quorum-sized vote counter.\",\n  \"status\": \"checked\",\n  \"previous_id\": null,\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"boundary_changes\": [],\n  \"obligation_checks\": {\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\": [\n    \"3c9d7e6ae7a04f4f9ce7a782e755960a\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [],\n  \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n  \"audit_question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"Can a leader that cannot reach a quorum of its configured voters still receive a successful VerifyLeader result because a configured non-voter answers the verification heartbeat?\",\n   \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader is documented as a guard against returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost; counting non-voter confirmations can let a separated leader confirm authority.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-suffrage\",\n    \"src-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-vote\",\n    \"src-notifyall\",\n    \"src-heartbeat\",\n    \"src-startstop\",\n    \"src-quorum\",\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader quorum\",\n    \"leader replication state\",\n    \"non-voter suffrage\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"leader with a committed mixed-voter configuration and a partitioned voter quorum\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> per-replication notify -> verification heartbeat -> notifyAll -> shared vote comparison\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [],\n   \"fact_ids\": [],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {},\n   \"obligation_relation_kind\": null,\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down later, but that separate timer does not mediate this VerifyLeader completion.\"\n   ],\n   \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Whether the surrounding deployment uses VerifyLeader as a linearizable-read guard.\",\n    \"How long a caller may act on a false confirmation before the separate lease check fires.\"\n   ],\n   \"trigger_rationale\": \"The source binds the documented stale-read guard and the suffrage distinction directly to the observed VerifyLeader completion path.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_limitations\": []\n }\n]\n==== question_candidates\n[\n {\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"id\": \"fb5c370c7acf451584b6ba19cc294a9d\",\n  \"question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"Can a leader that cannot reach a quorum of its configured voters still receive a successful VerifyLeader result because a configured non-voter answers the verification heartbeat?\",\n   \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader is documented as a guard against returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost; counting non-voter confirmations can let a separated leader confirm authority.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n